**Strategy for the locked-navigation test**
- Skim the whole section first if allowed; complete each question properly before moving on, since you cannot return.
- Budget time: roughly 120 minutes across SQL, 2 Java problems, 10 MCQs and the web tasks; do not sink 40 minutes into one question.

**Web tasks: approach.** The template is half-built, so read the HTML, CSS and JS files first and use the ids, class names and function names already there. Make small changes; do not rewrite the page.

**1. Link image sources.** Fix the `src` paths to match the real folder and file names, including case; add meaningful `alt` text.

```html
<img src="images/photo1.jpg" alt="Mountain view" id="photo1">
```

**2. Form validation.** Use HTML attributes (`required`, `type="email"`, `minlength`, `pattern`) and a JS check on submit.

```js
form.addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
  if (!nameInput.value.trim() || !/^\S+@\S+\.\S+$/.test(emailInput.value)) {
    e.preventDefault();
    errorMsg.textContent = "Please enter a valid name and email.";
  }
});
```

**3. Image showcase.** A main image plus thumbnails; clicking a thumbnail changes the main image.

```js
document.querySelectorAll(".thumb").forEach((t) =>
  t.addEventListener("click", () => { main.src = t.src; })
);
```

**4. onclick handlers.** Either `<button onclick="showNext()">` with a global function `showNext`, or `addEventListener`. Match what the template expects and check the function name spelling.

**Check before submitting:** open the browser console for errors, test each interaction, and confirm that ids and class names exactly match the task text.

**Other sections.** SQL: joins and aggregation (practise `GROUP BY`/`HAVING`). Java DSA: arrays, strings, hashing, two pointers. MCQs: OOP, collections, exceptions, String immutability.
